  "narrative": {
    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** Core cinema and venue project activity experienced a seasonally soft quarter, with slower customer spending pressuring legacy revenue, but this was partly offset by the first full-quarter contribution from the newly acquired DCS Cinema Loudspeaker line. The loudspeaker shipments not only provided a new revenue stream but also shifted the sales mix toward higher-margin products, improving profit quality. The broader out-of-home entertainment market appears stable, though project timing remains lumpy and subject to venue capex cycles.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Management moved quickly to integrate the DCS acquisition, generating immediate sales and demonstrating disciplined bolt-on M&A execution. Capital was deployed to build loudspeaker inventory to support the launch. The team is communicating transparently through earnings calls and emphasizing strategic growth even as legacy top-line faces headwinds, indicating a deliberate pivot toward higher-value product lines while maintaining core customer relationships.",
